# mail_filter -- whitelist IP addresses and CIDR ranges
# Messages from these source addresses bypass ALL filtering entirely --
# equivalent to Postfix's mynetworks, but evaluated independently by
# mail_filter.
#
# One entry per line: IPv4, IPv6, or CIDR notation.
# Lines beginning with # are comments. Empty lines are ignored.
#
# Accepted formats:
#   192.168.1.1           single IPv4 address
#   192.168.1.0/24        IPv4 CIDR range
#   ::1                   single IPv6 address
#   2001:db8::/32         IPv6 CIDR range
#
# Reload without restart:
#   service mail_filter reload      (FreeBSD)
#   systemctl reload mail_filter    (Linux)
#
# Recommended entries:
#   - All networks from Postfix mynetworks
#   - Your own relay servers (even if already in mynetworks)
#   - Authenticated submission servers (port 587 clients)
#   - Peer MX servers that relay to this host
#
# Note: this whitelist is independent of Postfix mynetworks.
